      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. The original has significant issues: dead code copied from an abstract base class with invalid generic `T` references and an abstract method declaration. I'll rewrite it cleanly with only what's needed for the actual test, plus clear explanations for the magic numbers.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all dead/broken code (invalid generic `T` references and the abstract method declaration) from the original, keeps only the minimal `createFilter` helper needed by the test, and adds explanatory comments clarifying why the magic hex values correspond to bits 63 and 64 straddling the boundary between the two longs."
